.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Anchored to the repository root on purpose. An unanchored `records/` would be
# harmless today, but the same mistake with a directory that shares a name with
# a source package would silently leave code out of every commit, and anchoring
# everything here keeps that class of bug impossible.
#
# `records/` holds the windows, and a window is production text. That is not an
# accident of the design — it is the design: an eval case IS the thing the
# customer wrote, and you cannot build a dataset out of text nobody kept. So the
# text is kept, redacted before it is written, mode 0600 under a 0700 directory,
# and never committed. This one line is the difference between a tool that
# handles personal data carefully and a repository that publishes it.
/records/

# `selected/` holds the shortlist, and a candidate carries the redacted case —
# which is still the thing a customer wrote, and the whole reason `records/` is
# ignored. `drift/` holds only counts, rates and cluster ids and quotes nothing,
# but it is a per-run artefact about a window that is itself ignored, and a
# comparison committed without the windows it compares is evidence of nothing.
/selected/
/drift/

# `goldens/` holds what `loghog emit` writes, and a drafted case IS the ticket:
# the golden-case schema's `input` field is the redacted text a customer wrote.
# `review-<window>.md` shows the same text on purpose, because a review of
# criteria without the case they came from is a spelling check. Both are
# therefore treated exactly like `records/` — the goldens file a person
# eventually promotes INTO is wherever they point `--into`, which is their
# repository's business rather than this one's.
#
# `health/` quotes nothing at all, but it is a per-run artefact about a window
# that is itself ignored, and a coverage figure committed without the window it
# was computed over is evidence of nothing.
/goldens/
/health/

# Per-run artifacts from anything later. Nothing writes here in Phase A; the
# rule is here so that the first stage that wants a scratch directory finds one
# already ignored rather than adding it to a commit and then to a .gitignore.
/runs/

# NOT ignored, on purpose: /mappings/, /samples/ and /logs/. A mapping is the
# record of how somebody's log was interpreted, and a window whose mapping is not
# in the repository is a window nobody can reproduce. The samples and the two
# demo windows are invented — every name, address and card number in them was
# made up for the purpose — and each directory says so on the first line of its
# own README.
